'2025-11-21 12:13:28','2025-11-21 12:13:28',1,0,NULL),(238,4,36054,36183,'lightblue','1 percent of GDP (Table 1), contributes 30\npercent of export earnings and employs 75 percent of the total labor force\n(URT, 2013)','2025-11-21 12:13:28','2025-11-21 12:13:28',1,0,NULL),(239,4,39367,39629,'lightblue','It has\nbeen identified as one of the priority sub-sectors in the National Export\nStrategy (2008), the Kilimo Kwanza Resolution and a key component in the\ndiversification of the agricultural sector from over dependence on traditional\nprimary agricultural products','2025-11-21 12:13:28','2025-11-21 12:13:28',1,0,NULL),(240,4,39942,40024,'lightblue','the country is thought to have\nstarted exporting bean seed to Europe in the 1950s)','2025-11-21 12:13:28','2025-11-21 12:13:28',1,0,NULL),(241,4,40116,40199,'lightblue','Local and\nforeign investors endow the floriculture and export vegetables sub-sector','2025-11-21 12:13:28','2025-11-21 12:13:28',1,0,NULL),(242,4,66229,66599,'lightblue','In addition, the Government in collaboration with DPs and private sector have\nput in place measures aimed at improving the flow of finance and investment\nto the agriculture sector such as: the Export Credit Guarantee Scheme, USAID\nGuarantee for Input Scheme, Private Agriculture Sector Support (PASS), the\nAgro-Dealers Scheme and the Agriculture Input Trust Fund (AGIFT)','2025-11-21 12:13:28','2025-11-21 12:13:28',1,0,NULL),(243,4,99510,99666,'lightblue','2     Output 2: Export of non-traditional agricultural commodities by\n            men and women smallholders increased by 50 percent by 2025\n\nActions:\n\n   1','2025-11-21 12:13:28','2025-11-21 12:13:28',1,0,NULL),(244,4,99811,99910,'lightblue','Design sustainable programmes to support the certification of\n      smallholders for export markets','2025-11-21 12:13:28','2025-11-21 12:13:28',1,0,NULL),(245,4,100292,100427,'lightblue','Promote the adoption of grading and standardization systems for all\n      agricultural commodities for both domestic and export markets','2025-11-21 12:13:28','2025-11-21 12:13:28',1,0,NULL),(246,4,153261,155855,'lightblue','Value and Quantity of Marketed\n                                 output of food and cash crops,\n                                 livestock and fish products by\n                                 smallholders\n\n\n    61\n                                           Tanzania Climate Smart Agriculture Program 2015 - 2025\n\n\n\n\n                                           Verifiable Indicators              Source of Verification               Assumptions\n\n                                   Value of Export of non-traditional\n                                   agricultural commodities by men and\n                                   women smallholders\n\n                                   Established Grading and\n                                   standardization systems of\n                                   agricultural commodities\n\nComponent 4: Research for Development and Innovations\n\nGenerated and disseminated         Hectares of land managed under           Quarterly Reports              Agricultural research in\nimproved land management           climate-resilient practices              Publications                    support of CSA\nand gender sensitive climate                                                Mass media                     Conducive policy\nresilient agricultural practices   Number of CSA technologies               Evaluation Reports              environment maintained\nand technologies in targeted       developed                                Annual survey reports\nareas                                                                       Annual Reports\n                                   Increased funding in research and        Mid Term Reports\n                                   development and innovations              Review Missions\n                                                                    