              of the project.\\\\n\\\\n    This is different from the Tanzanian\\\\n    situation where such people are not\\\\n    entitled to any assistance.\\\\nTypes of affected Persons\\/Lost      Tanzanian Law                            World Bank OP 4.12                        Comparison\\/Gaps\\\\nAssets\\\\nLand Users                          Tanzania law on compulsory               WB OP 4.12 includes displaced\\\\n                                    acquisition and compensation is          persons who have no recognizable\\\\n                                    limited to those who can prove de jure   legal right or claim to the land they\\\\n                                    or de facto land ownership. Users are    are occupying\\\\n                                    not covered\\\\nOwners of non-permanent buildings   Tanzanian law makes no                   Under OP 4.12 permanent and non-          The gap between Tanzanian law and\\\\nOwners of permanent buildings       differentiation between owners of        permanent buildings need to be            WB OP 4.12 is about eligibility, which\\\\n                                    permanent and non-permanent              compensated.                              hinges upon formal or informal\\\\n                                    buildings. As long as ownership can                                                ownership.\\\\n                                    be proved compensation is payable.       Where displaced persons have no\\\\n                                                                             recognizable legal rights they are to     In Tanzania compensation is based on\\\\n                                    Determination of compensation is         be provided with resettlement             market value, determined using the\\\\n                                    based on the market value of the         assistance in lieu of compensation for    depreciated replacement cost\\\\n 